  "extraction_method": "Per-column median across the filled 52'\" slit of _crj (CR-SPLIT sets) or _flt (single exposures) counts divided by exposure time; DQ exclusion mask (lost data | bad detector | aperture feature | saturation) = 4110; wavelengths from the _sx1/_x1d solutions, audited against the image headers",
  "literature_correction_convention": {
    "paper": "Youngblood et al. 2020 Sec. II.2: CalSTIS flt -> L.A.Cosmic -> x2d -> median across the cross-dispersion direction excluding flagged pixels; in-eclipse spectrum divided by an average of out-of-eclipse spectra; no absolute flux calibration for the transmission spectra",
    "reproduced_here": "Same median extraction on _crj/_flt without x2d rectification (the filled slit spans the full detector height, so rectification cannot change a full-height median); CR handling via the pipeline _crj instead of L.A.Cosmic",
    "omitted_with_bounds": [
      "Lommel-Seeliger per-exposure division: F_LS in 0.4975-0.5021 with closely coupled incidence/emission angles, <=1% effect on in/out ratios",
      "Penumbral-only limb-darkening division: G430L I/I0 0.7-0.79; published penumbral ratios are therefore about 1/0.75 above the raw ratios here"
    ],
    "published_cross_check": "No machine-readable published spectrum exists; the paper's umbral statements used here are qualitative anchors, checked where noted: 'no photons <=4200 A' is checked against the blue_end metrics; 'umbral G430L S/N 60-120' and 'Chappuis-band O3 detection >4000 A' are recorded as unchecked anchors (no corresponding mechanical check here)"
  },
