  "probe_scope": "+/-150 km sampled displacement mirrors the December 2011 radial probe; the track-error envelope cases (+/-1042 km, Youngblood et al. pointing budget) bracket the same-region premise symmetrically and are recorded, not folded into the headline metrics. Snapshot stores per-case quantitative-window summaries; full-resolution probe curves are regenerable byte-identically via run_analysis",
  "limitations": [
    "Pointing wanders within the paper's documented budget (up to 10 arcmin track approximation error), so in/out sampled lunar regions can differ; lunar albedo cancellation is conditional on the published mean linear-track coordinates and degrades within the recorded envelope",
    "The model treats the solar disk as uniform; the paper's solar center-to-limb residual applies to the umbral branch uncorrected (paper: possible factor <=2 on umbral transmission spectra)",
    "No background/scattered-light subtraction; STIS CCD long-wavelength scattered light adds a broad pedestal that only partially cancels in the in/out ratio, as in the paper",
    "G430L ends at 570 nm and the model tables start at 300 nm: no red-end Chappuis core and no 289-300 nm edge; turquoise-band color claims are outside this source's reach",
    "Auxiliary penumbral branch omits the published limb-darkening division; see its scope field"
  ],
